 "title": "ATP synthase (chloroplast)",
 "shows": "ATP synthase in the thylakoid membrane, drawn from its real structure: the rotor, a ring of subunits in the membrane; the internal rod, rising from the ring into the catalytic knob in the stroma; and the stator, a stalk anchored in the membrane beside the knob that holds it still. Protons wait in the thylakoid space above the membrane.",
 "use_for": "lessons on how chloroplasts make ATP: the light reactions, chemiosmosis, the proton gradient across the thylakoid membrane. It is the chloroplast's enzyme and its compartments are the thylakoid space and the stroma, so it does not fit a lesson set in mitochondria.",
